From 582bc92e414ae5d12dc6edad8d0de29465e7c7dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Johannes=20Br=C3=BCderl?= <johannes.bruederl@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:15:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(transport): let a caller write its frame when the writer
 is idle

Every SendFrame/SendFrameContext woke writeLoop and then waited for its
acknowledgment: two goroutine handoffs per GRV and commit. When nothing is
queued and writeLoop is not mid-batch, the caller now writes the frame
itself under writeMu; otherwise it queues as before, so frames never
overtake queued ones and concurrent senders still coalesce. A flush with
nothing queued returns at once. Deferred (pipelined) frames still queue.
---
